<dtccode/>
<dtcname>Starter system</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM0000029LS00NX_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000DE500000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>The cranking hold control system energizes the starter until the engine control computer, having detected the starter signal (STSW) from the main body ECU, determines that the engine has started.</ptxt>
<ptxt>When the starter signal (STSW) is input, the engine control computer outputs the ACC cut relay signal (ACCR) to the main body ECU and turns ON the ST CUT relay to prevent flickering of the meter, clock, audio, etc., and the engine control computer outputs a signal to the STAR terminal.</ptxt>
<ptxt>The STAR output signal turns ON the ST relay via the neutral start switch and operates the starter. Also, while the engine is being cranked, the starter operation signal is also sent to the STA terminal of the engine control computer. The main body ECU monitors the voltage of the ST CUT relay output side terminal, and protects or drives the starter circuit if there is a malfunction.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A153079J03" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</item>
</list1>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000029LS00NX_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000DE600000">
